# No `.sh` file extensions

Tracked bash entrypoints and sourced libraries in this repo **must not** use a `.sh` suffix.

## Do

- Name scripts like repository-helpers: `provision_init_files`, `bootstrap_host`, `lib/tool_path`, `cursor/statusline`, `tests/foo.test`
- Keep a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang on executables; for sourced libs use `# shellcheck shell=bash` (no shebang required)
- Update all source paths, docs, CI globs, and Cursor rules when renaming

## Do not

- Add new `*.sh` files under this clone
- Rename only some call sites and leave stale `lib/foo.sh` references

## Exceptions (not our files)

Leave upstream / host paths alone when they already use `.sh`:

- Homebrew / distro `bash_completion.sh`, `nvm.sh`, vendor `install.sh` URLs
- Legacy host state such as `~/.config/init-files/tools.sh` (still read for migration)

## Examples

```bash
# ❌ BAD
. "${clone}/lib/tool_path.sh"
command="${clone}/cursor/statusline.sh"

# ✅ GOOD
. "${clone}/lib/tool_path"
command="${clone}/cursor/statusline"
```
